 "intro": "At Leucopetra on the Isthmus of Corinth, 146 BC, the same year Carthage fell. The Achaean League has defied Rome. You are the consul Lucius Mummius.",
 "debrief": "Pausanias and other writers report that the Achaeans, encouraged by a small success, came out to fight at Leucopetra. Their cavalry fled at the first Roman charge, and a flank attack by a thousand picked men broke their infantry. Diaeus fled and later killed himself. Mummius waited before entering the nearly empty city of Corinth, which on the Senate’s orders was destroyed and its art shipped to Rome. Greece came under Roman rule. The other choices are what-ifs.",
